{
  // Type coverage for the TOP LEVEL of `scripts/`.
  //
  // `scripts/build/tsconfig.json` covers `scripts/build/**` and
  // `scripts/cdp/tsconfig.json` covers the CDP driver, but until this file
  // existed nothing typechecked `scripts/*.ts` — and `typecheck:all` walks the
  // ten packages then ends in `typecheck:build-scripts`
  // (`cd scripts/build && tsc -p tsconfig.json`), so the top level of
  // `scripts/` was outside the type gate. That is the directory that holds the
  // repo's own guards: `check-coverage-map.ts`, `ios-wire-enum-parity.ts`,
  // `check-i18n-parity.ts`, `ipc-inventory.ts`, `sort-locales.ts`. The
  // directory holding our checks was the one directory our checks did not
  // cover.
  //
  // Wired into the root `typecheck:all` as `typecheck:scripts`.
  //
  // `ipc-inventory.ts` and its reader `ipc-inventory.test.ts` are NOT excluded
  // from coverage — both are covered by `tsconfig.ipc-inventory.json`, which is
  // run by the same `typecheck:scripts` entry. They cannot live in THIS
  // program: they import `RPC_CHANNELS` from
  // `apps/electron/src/shared/types.ts`, which drags that file (and
  // `packages/shared` behind it) into whatever program compiles it.
  // Checked under these flags rather than its own app's, app source reports
  // errors about flags it was never written against (measured: one TS2345 in
  // `types.ts` that exists only because `tsconfig.base.json` enables
  // `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` and `apps/electron/tsconfig.json` does not).
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["bun", "node"]
  },
  // `platform-rig/*.ts` (P6.781). The rig sits one directory down, so the
  // top-level glob missed all three of its files and the P3.190 orphan sweep in
  // `check-typecheck-coverage.ts` reported `run-linux-removal-probe.test.ts` as
  // a test file in no program at all. Measured before widening, with a throwaway
  // config over `platform-rig/*.ts` alone: **0 errors** across
  // `removal-corpus.ts`, `run-linux-removal-probe.ts` and
  // `run-linux-removal-probe.test.ts`, with a planted `const x: number = "s"` in
  // `removal-corpus.ts` reported as TS2322 to prove the probe was reading them.
  // So nothing here is excluded and nothing was fixed to make it fit.
  //
  // NOT `**/*.ts`: `build/` and `cdp/` have their own tsconfigs, and this file's
  // header records what compiling a surface under another program's flags costs.
  // A NEW subdirectory under `scripts/` would be missed the same way this one
  // was — the orphan sweep is what catches that, not a wider glob here.
  "include": ["*.ts", "platform-rig/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["ipc-inventory.ts", "ipc-inventory.test.ts"]
}
